MTLCommonCounter is typedef'd as `NSString * const`, so Dawn's `std::vector<MTLCommonCounter>`
has a const-qualified element type. That was always ill-formed, but libc++ only began
rejecting it outright in the Xcode 16.3 SDK, whose std::allocator carries an unconditional
`static_assert(!is_const<T>::value)` with no escape macro and no _LIBCPP_STD_VER guard. The
headers ship with the SDK rather than the compiler, so this cannot be worked around by
swapping in an older clang alone. The parameter is only ever read, so dropping the top-level
const off the element type is behaviour-preserving.

Drop this patch if the pinned Dawn revision is ever bumped past upstream's own fix.

